{
  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "49fd95ba2b463c1501f57d762c31bb9c60902eb78fc5c79ad07c101bfa0c29a1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-49fd95ba2b46-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The case arose from an incident in which Edward\u202fCaniglia, during an argument with his wife at their Rhode Island home, retrieved a handgun, placed it on the dining\u2011room table, and asked his wife to shoot him; she declined and left for a hotel."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justices Kagan and Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 58,
              "start": 58
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The legal question presented concerned what standard governs warrantless entry into a home under the \u201ccommunity caretaking\u201d exception\u2014whether probable cause, reasonable suspicion, or a lower standard applies."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background and Question",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "case_id": "2020-20-157",
  "decision": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "49fd95ba2b463c1501f57d762c31bb9c60902eb78fc5c79ad07c101bfa0c29a1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-49fd95ba2b46-0000-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that the First Circuit\u2019s \u201ccommunity caretaking\u201d rule exceeds the scope of the Fourth Amendment."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "49fd95ba2b463c1501f57d762c31bb9c60902eb78fc5c79ad07c101bfa0c29a1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-49fd95ba2b46-0000-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The judgment of the lower court was vacated and the case was remanded for further proceedings consistent with this opinion."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "49fd95ba2b463c1501f57d762c31bb9c60902eb78fc5c79ad07c101bfa0c29a1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-49fd95ba2b46-0000-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito filed a concurring opinion."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "49fd95ba2b463c1501f57d762c31bb9c60902eb78fc5c79ad07c101bfa0c29a1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-49fd95ba2b46-0001-0000",
              "ev-49fd95ba2b46-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 13,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kavanaugh, justices Kavanaugh (joined by others) filed a concurring opinion that rejected the broad \u201ccommunity caretaking\u201d theory and affirmed the exigent\u2011circumstances doctrine."
      }
    ],
