  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Shay Dvoretzky",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Shay Dvoretzky, shay\u202fDvoretzky emphasized that the Fourth Amendment protects the sanctity of the home and that the government may enter only with a warrant, consent, or exigent circumstances."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Dvoretzky",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Dvoretzky, he discussed the emergency\u2011aid doctrine as covering true emergencies when there is reasonable cause to believe someone is in need."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Dvoretzky",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Dvoretzky, he noted that the respondents have not argued exigent circumstances and have effectively waived them."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kagan asked what standard governs the laws\u2014probable cause or something lower? Could it be something lower?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 54,
              "start": 54
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer expressed concern that a broad caretaker exception could be limitless and sought subsidiary standards."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 58,
              "start": 58
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, justice Alito questioned what level of government information is required\u2014probable cause, reasonable suspicion, or something else?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "49fd95ba2b463c1501f57d762c31bb9c60902eb78fc5c79ad07c101bfa0c29a1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-49fd95ba2b46-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 13,
              "start": 13
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kavanaugh, justice Kavanaugh reiterated the exigent\u2011circumstances doctrine, which permits warrantless entry in emergencies such as fighting a fire, preventing destruction of evidence, hot pursuit, threats to safety, emergency assistance, or protecting a threatened occupant."
      }
    ],
