              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Ratner, the amicus argues that this case differs from most Fourth Amendment cases because the issue is whether to act immediately or not at all, and suggests the \u201ccommunity caretaking\u201d label is misleading."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Ratner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "2bf2f7c70d0e6b59408c3bc5685da5b531e5402d66bd3f22edd7fef2c9c7d9c6",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-2bf2f7c70d0e-0003-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 76,
                "start": 76
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Ratner, it further proposes that the rule should require specific facts establishing a non\u2011investigatory justification and that the official\u2019s actions be reasonably tailored to that interest."
        }
